          "derivation": "OP ud- 'up' appears unchanged before a vowel in ud-apatatā 'rose up (in rebellion)' (DB). OP uzma- 'stake' (only in uzmayā-patiy kar- 'to impale', DB 2.76 etc.) is analysed by Kent as *ud-zma- 'that which is up from the earth', from ud- + zma-, the zero grade of zam- 'earth', with total assimilation of d. Nourai's gloss 'grown up from ground' paraphrases this. Kent notes rival analyses (Wackernagel, Lommel, König), but his is the standard one.",
